  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 319 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nHigh pressure starts to reinforce itself across the region\nthroughout this weekend. This will start the return of hot and \ndry conditions once again. High temperatures near 104 degrees are\nforecast across the Big Country on Saturday. Similar conditions \nwill continue into the early part of next week, but with slightly \ncooler temperatures. Long range models continue to show a weakened\nhigh pressure ridge by the middle to end of next week. This may \nallow for cooler temperatures and a few low chances (20%) for \nrain. This remains rather uncertain at this point, however.",
